{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class ar {\n    static BufferedReader reader;\n    static StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n    static Map<Integer, Integer> costMap;\n    static int[] values;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        try {\n            solve();\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            e.printStackTrace();\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void solve() throws Exception {\n        int n = nextInt(), budget = nextInt();\n        values = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            values[i] = nextInt();\n        }\n\n        if (n % 2 != 0) {\n            System.out.print(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        costMap = new HashMap<>();\n        int evenCount = 0, oddCount = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (values[i] % 2 == 0) evenCount++;\n            else oddCount++;\n            if (evenCount > 0 && oddCount > 0 && evenCount == oddCount && i + 1 < n) {\n                costMap.put(i, Math.abs(values[i] - values[i + 1]));\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (costMap.size() == 0) {\n            System.out.print(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        List<Integer> costs = new ArrayList<>(costMap.values());\n        Collections.sort(costs);\n\n        if (costs.size() == 1) {\n            System.out.println(costs.get(0) <= budget ? 1 : 0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        int count = 0;\n        for (int c : costs) {\n            if (c <= budget) {\n                budget -= c;\n                count++;\n            } else {\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.print(count);\n    }\n\n    static String next() throws Exception {\n        while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreElements()) {\n            tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(reader.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokenizer.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    static int nextInt() throws Exception {\n        return Integer.parseInt(next());\n    }\n\n    static long nextLong() throws Exception {\n        return Long.parseLong(next());\n    }\n\n    static double nextDouble() throws Exception {\n        return Double.parseDouble(next());\n    }\n\n    static String nextLine() throws Exception {\n        return reader.readLine();\n    }\n}\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nstatic map<int, int> costMap;\nstatic vector<int> values;\n\nstatic string nextToken;\nstatic istringstream tokenizer;\n\nstatic string next() {\n    string token;\n    if (!(tokenizer >> token)) {\n        string line;\n        getline(cin, line);\n        tokenizer.str(line);\n        tokenizer.clear();\n        tokenizer >> token;\n    }\n    return token;\n}\n\nstatic int nextInt() {\n    return stoi(next());\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = nextInt(), budget = nextInt();\n    values.resize(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        values[i] = nextInt();\n    }\n\n    if (n % 2 != 0) {\n        cout << 0;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    costMap.clear();\n    int evenCount = 0, oddCount = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (values[i] % 2 == 0) evenCount++;\n        else oddCount++;\n        if (evenCount > 0 && oddCount > 0 && evenCount == oddCount && i + 1 < n) {\n            costMap[i] = abs(values[i] - values[i + 1]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (costMap.size() == 0) {\n        cout << 0;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    vector<int> costs;\n    for (auto& p : costMap) {\n        costs.push_back(p.second);\n    }\n    sort(costs.begin(), costs.end());\n\n    if (costs.size() == 1) {\n        cout << (costs[0] <= budget ? 1 : 0);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    int count = 0;\n    for (int c : costs) {\n        if (c <= budget) {\n            budget -= c;\n            count++;\n        } else {\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << count;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00024923557066358626, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0005241450853645802, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.004014529287815094, -9.536738616588991e-07, -8.940656698541716e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.041205719113349915, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.01418977603316307, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.602820692729438e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.24540828168392181, -0.005929143168032169, -0.005929261911660433, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -0.3914054334163666, -0.008616885170340538, -0.0008055302896536887, -5.245195097813848e-06, -0.0038689535576850176, -0.07889734953641891, -0.016265662387013435, -1.108640208258